fix(openflow): request all ports in PORT_DESC; pin FDB before flow install

Re-implements the intent of 106a0ef6 on current HEAD, where the plumbing that
commit relied on no longer exists (handle_connection lost its static_fdb
parameter, the barrier block is gone, and the controller had been moved back to
Version::Of13). Do not force-merge 106a0ef6 -- it conflicts around hunk 2.

Root cause of the flooding: OF1.5 added an ofp15_port_desc_request body that
OF1.3 does not have (openflow-1.5.h: "All ports if OFPP_ANY").
build_port_desc_request sent an 8-byte body, so port_no was absent/zero -- port
0 is not a valid port, OVS answers with an EMPTY port list and no error, every
symbolic port name fails to resolve, every configured flow is skipped and
actions=NORMAL floods gateway-bound frames to every port. Observed on the wire:

  OFPST_PORT_DESC request (OF1.5) (xid=0x4): port=0
  OFPST_PORT_DESC reply   (OF1.5) (xid=0x4):      <- empty

Changes:

- OF_VERSION const (Version::Of15) replaces the hardcoded Version::Of13 at
  every send site. OF1.5 is load-bearing, not cosmetic: packet_type matches and
  encap(ethernet) -- needed to give the L3-only netmaker WireGuard port an
  Ethernet header -- do not exist before 1.5. One constant, so a bridge pinned
  to an older protocol set can be accommodated with a single edit.
- build_port_desc_request: 16-byte body with OFPP_ANY at body[8..12], and the
  stale pad(12) doc comment corrected to the real
  type(2)+flags(2)+pad(4)+port_no(4)+pad(4) layout.
- discover_ports: stride on each ofp_port's own length field instead of a fixed
  64-byte chunk. From OF1.4 ofp_port is variable length (40-byte fixed part plus
  port properties), so the OF1.3 stride mis-slices every port after the first.
  Also harvests hw_addr into a port name -> MAC map so static flows can say
  "eth_dst": "port_mac:ovsbr0" instead of hard-coding the bridge MAC.
- Static FDB pins are re-asserted as step 5b, BEFORE the static-flow loop and
  its barrier. The pins live in ovs-vswitchd's L2 table (not OVSDB, not the flow
  table) so a vswitchd restart drops them, and the ISP filters VRRP off customer
  ports so the gateway virtual MAC can never be learned. L2 reachability must
  never be gated on symbolic-port resolution. Adds the plumbing the reference
  commit assumed: OpenFlowController::static_fdb populated from
  static_fdb_from_env(), threaded through run() into handle_connection.
- Static-flow loop counts skips (static_skipped) and logs each one with warn!.
  The plugin declares atomic_operations: false; one unresolvable flow (netmaker,
  while netmaker-ovs-attach is broken) must not tear down the session.
- Re-adds the post-install barrier so static-flow acceptance is deterministic,
  with the non-hanging semantics: FlowMod errors warn! instead of bail!, the
  loop breaks when an error carries our own barrier_xid (an errored barrier
  never produces a reply), and a 10s tokio::time::timeout bounds the wait.

Adds test_port_desc_request_asks_for_all_ports. The two existing FlowMod tests
now assert version byte 0x06.
